   "evidence": "In the `{i,j}` block, `transvectionWeylElement hij = !![0,1;-1,0]`, so its inverse is `!![0,-1;1,0] = transvectionWeylElement hij.symm`; algebraically `x_{ij}(-1)x_{ji}(1)x_{ij}(-1) = !![0,-1;1,0] = x_{ji}(1)x_{ij}(-1)x_{ji}(1)`, i.e. `transvectionWeylElement_inv hij` (line 261) equals `transvectionWeylElement_def hij.symm` (line 255). Instantiating line 268 with `hij.symm`, `hjk := hik`, `hik := hjk` yields verbatim the statement at line 338 (and symmetrically for lines 304/348).",
   "file": "TauCeti/LinearAlgebra/Matrix/GeneralLinearGroup/Transvection.lean",
